.TH KB_DIO_RESET_COUNTER 2 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
KB_DIO_RESET_COUNTER \- Reset counter and encoder values of a DIO, DI, or MIO
expansion module in the piControl driver

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.B "#include <sys/ioctl.h>"
.sp
.BI "int ioctl(int " fd ", KB_DIO_RESET_COUNTER, SDIOResetCounter *" argp ");"
.sp
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.sp
.B "typedef struct SDIOResetCounterStr SDIOResetCounter;"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
Reset all counters and encoders of a DIO, DI or MIO expansion module to their
initial value of
.BR 0 .

The
.I i8uAddress
field of the
.BR SDIOResetCounter (2type)
struct is set to the address of the module, while the
.I i16uBitfield
field is a mask of the configured inputs that should be reset to their initial
value.

If a counter is configured on input
.I I_3
and an encoder is configured on the
inputs
.IR I_6 " and " I_7 ,
then bits 2 and 5 must be set to
.B 1
and
.I i16uBitfield
must be set to the value
.BR 0x0024 .

.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.

On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.

.SH ERRORS
Error codes set in
.I errno
can be, among others, one of the following:
.TP
.B EAGAIN
A driver reset is in progress.
.TP
.B EFAULT
Failure on copying values to/from caller.
.TP
.B EOPNOTSUPP
The RevPi does not support expansion modules.
.TP
.B EINVAL
No DIO, DI, or MIO module with the given address was found, or the value of the
field
.I i16uBitfield
of the
.BR SDIOResetCounter (2type)
struct is
.BR 0 .

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioctl (2),
.BR SDIOResetCounter (2type),
.BR piControl (4)
